<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta name="description" content="S'Up for Slack Teams facilitates informal standups and coffee meetings by creating fresh triads of teammates every week.">
    <meta property="og:title" content="S'Up for Slack Teams - Generate Fresh Triads of Team Members to Meet for Coffee Every Week">
    <meta property="og:description" content="Bring teammates together with fresh groups of three for coffee, informal standups, and better connections in Slack.">
    <meta name="twitter:title" content="S'Up for Slack Teams - Generate Fresh Triads of Team Members to Meet for Coffee Every Week">
    <meta name="twitter:description" content="Bring teammates together with fresh groups of three for coffee, informal standups, and better connections in Slack.">
    <meta name="keywords" content="slack,scrum,standup,triads,teams,organizations,donut,coffee">
    <title>S'Up for Slack Teams - Generate Fresh Triads of Team Members to Meet for Coffee Every Week</title>
    <%= partial 'public/partials/_head.html.erb' %>
    <script type="application/ld+json">
    {
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "SoftwareApplication",
      "name": "S'Up for Slack Teams",
      "url": "<%= SlackRubyBotServer::Service.url %>",
      "applicationCategory": "BusinessApplication",
      "operatingSystem": "Slack",
      "description": "S'Up for Slack Teams facilitates informal standups and coffee meetings by creating fresh triads of teammates every week."
    }
    </script>
  </head>
  <body id="page-top" class="site-page">
    <%= partial 'public/partials/_navigation.html.erb' %>
    <main id="main">
      <div id="homepage">
        <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
          <div class="page-container">
            <div class="hero-copy">
              <h1 id="hero-title">Meet for coffee.<br>Three teammates at a time.</h1>
              <p class="hero-description">Help employees turn casual conversations into their next collaboration. S'Up generates fresh triads every week for an informal standup.</p>
              <div class="hero-actions">
                <%= partial 'public/partials/_install_button.html.erb' %>
                <a class="hero-link" href="#howtouse">See how it works</a>
              </div>
              <p class="trial-note">Free for 3 weeks. No credit card needed.</p>
            </div>
            <figure class="hero-preview">
              <img src="/img/sup-dm.png" width="2292" height="1664" alt="S'Up introducing three teammates in a Slack conversation">
              <figcaption class="team-count"><span id="tagline" style="display: none;">Bringing teams together, one coffee at a time.</span></figcaption>
            </figure>
          </div>
        </section>
        <section class="homepage-section page-container" id="howtouse" aria-labelledby="how-title">
          <h2 id="how-title">How it works</h2>
          <ol class="setup-steps">
            <li><h3>Invite the bot</h3><p>First, add S'Up to your workspace and invite it to a Slack channel. Each channel has its own introductions and settings.</p></li>
            <li><h3>Meet for coffee</h3><p>It will then generate fresh triads of members of the Slack channel to meet for coffee every week in an informal standup, or <i>S'Up</i>.</p></li>
            <li><h3>Get it on the calendar</h3><p>It also introduces itself to new team members and can help set up a Google Calendar meeting.</p></li>
          </ol>
          <p class="setup-help"><a href="/help.html">Explore the commands &amp; FAQ</a></p>
        </section>
        <section class="followup-section" aria-labelledby="solution-title">
          <div class="page-container followup-layout">
            <div class="followup-copy">
              <h2 id="solution-title">You haven't tried 3.</h2>
              <p>Two people create one connection. Three people create three in the same meeting. <a href="https://medium.com/artsy-blog/what-sup-using-triads-to-develop-tribal-leadership-a01d4f207bf8">Artsy</a> has used S'Up continuously since 2014.</p>
            </div>
            <figure class="followup-preview solution-preview">
              <img src="/img/sup-triad.png" width="700" height="212" alt="S'Up introducing three coworkers in Slack and inviting them to discuss what they are working on" loading="lazy">
            </figure>
          </div>
        </section>
        <section class="followup-section" aria-labelledby="followup-title">
          <div class="page-container followup-layout">
            <div class="followup-copy">
              <h2 id="followup-title">See introductions turn into meetings.</h2>
              <p>S'Up follows up a few days later to ask whether each group met, so you can track participation, not just introductions.</p>
            </div>
            <figure class="followup-preview">
              <img src="/img/sup-ask.png" width="475" height="115" alt="S'Up asking how a meeting went, with We All Met, Some of Us Met, and We Couldn't Meet buttons" loading="lazy">
            </figure>
          </div>
        </section>
        <section class="followup-section" aria-labelledby="reporting-title">
          <div class="page-container followup-layout">
            <div class="followup-copy">
              <h2 id="reporting-title">Show it's working.</h2>
              <p>S&rsquo;Up collects meeting feedback automatically, giving you participation and outcome numbers to share.</p>
              <p>Use <code>@sup stats</code> for channel statistics and <code>@sup rounds</code> to review individual rounds, right in Slack.</p>
            </div>
            <figure class="followup-preview reporting-preview">
              <img src="/img/sup-stats.png" width="690" height="101" alt="S'Up channel statistics in Slack showing the introduction schedule, opt-in rate, positive meeting outcomes, and response rate" loading="lazy">
            </figure>
          </div>
        </section>
        <section class="pricing-section page-container" id="pricing" aria-labelledby="pricing-title">
          <div>
            <h2 id="pricing-title">A small investment<br>in a more connected team.</h2>
            <p>You can try S'Up for free for 3 weeks without a credit card or personal info.</p>
            <p>You can unsubscribe any time by DMing the bot <code>unsubscribe</code>.</p>
            <a href="/help.html#support">Questions? We're here to help.</a>
          </div>
          <div class="pricing-action">
            <p class="section-label">Simple pricing</p>
            <p class="price"><strong>$39.99</strong><span>per team / year</span></p>
            <%= partial 'public/partials/_install_button.html.erb' %>
          </div>
        </section>
        <section class="project-info page-container" id="oss" aria-labelledby="source-title">
          <div>
            <h2 id="source-title">Open by design.</h2>
            <p>MIT-licensed Ruby code. Built in the open.<br><a href="https://github.com/dblock/slack-sup2">Explore the project on GitHub</a>.</p>
          </div>
          <div id="api">
            <h3>Your data stays yours.</h3>
            <p>Download CSV with <code>@sup data</code>, or use the <a href="<%= SlackRubyBotServer::Service.api_url %>">API</a>.<br><a href="https://github.com/dblock/slack-sup2/blob/main/API.md">Documentation</a> &middot; <a href="https://github.com/dblock/slack-sup2/tree/main/samples">Examples</a></p>
          </div>
        </section>
      </div>
      <section id="register" class="page-container registration-panel" style="display: none;" aria-labelledby="register-title">
        <h1 id="register-title">Connect your Slack team</h1>
        <p id="messages" role="status" aria-live="polite">Working, please wait ...</p>
        <p>Having trouble? <a href="mailto:dblock@vestris.com">Contact support</a> or <a href="/">return to S'Up</a>.</p>
      </section>
    </main>
    <%= partial 'public/partials/_footer.html.erb' %>
    <%= partial 'public/partials/_scripts.html' %>
    <script src="/js/register.js"></script>
    <script src="/js/stats.js"></script>
    <script src="/js/uptime.js"></script>
  </body>
</html>
